[{:registry/operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit], :registry/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger], :actor/scope-excluded-ops [:finalize-garment-construction :finalize-garment-construction-execution-decision :declare-workshop-safety-cleared :declare-safety-clearance :override-shop-safety-officer-judgment :override-safety-officer-judgment], :actor/robotics? true, :adr/related ["2799007319-cloud-itonami-isco-7319-handicraft-workers-nec-coverage" "2799007317-cloud-itonami-isco-7317-handicraft-workers-wood-basketry-coverage" "2799007211-cloud-itonami-isco-7211-metal-moulders-coremakers-coverage"], :adr/status :accepted, :actor/scope-excluded-terms ["finalize the garment construction" "finalize the garment construction execution decision" "proceed with the garment construction" "authorize the garment construction" "declare the workshop safety cleared" "declare the workshop safety-cleared" "declare safety-cleared" "declare workshop-safety-cleared" "override the shop safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override shop safety officer judgment"], :adr/id 2799007531, :phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}}}", :actor/domain :manufacturing/tailoring-workshop-scheduling-logistics-coordination, :actor/proposal-ops [:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order], :actor/hard-checks [:artisan-verified :workshop-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion], :registry/maturity :implemented, :actor/isco-08 "7531", :actor/always-escalate-ops [:flag-safety-concern], :adr/doc_type "adr", :operation/nodes [:intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold], :operation/entry-point :intake, :adr/body "# ADR 2799007531: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7531 Tailors, Dressmakers, Furriers and Hatters workshop scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7531\n-- Tailors, Dressmakers, Furriers and Hatters** only, Wave3\n(production/trades) of the rollout.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7531\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"7531\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Tailors, Dressmakers, Furriers and\nHatters\" -- confirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the\nentry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies\n[:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no\nrepository existed at `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7531` (`gh\napi` 404 confirmed before scaffolding). This ADR and its companion\nregistry edit promote the `7531` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nISCO-08 7531 covers four related needle-work trades: tailors,\ndressmakers, furriers and hatters. Standard workshop safety hazards\napply across all four -- needle injury, cutting-tool (shears) injury,\nsewing-machine/equipment-condition hazards -- without a single\ndominant hazard type, so this actor's hazard-escalation vocabulary is\ndeliberately generic (needle-hazard / cutting-tool-hazard /\nequipment-condition) rather than technique-specific to any one trade.\nFurriers specifically also raise material-provenance/handling\nconsiderations for pelt materials; this actor does not make sourcing,\nethical-provenance or quality determinations about pelt materials\nitself -- provenance recording is a workshop-registration concern\n(independently verified workshop) and a `:coordinate-supply-order`\nproposal for fabric/pelt/millinery materials is gated by the same\nordinary cost-threshold escalation as any other supply order, never by\nan autonomous provenance judgment. The controlling constraint for this\nvertical is that the closed op allowlist must NEVER include any op\nthat directly finalizes a garment-construction-execution decision\n(e.g. deciding a garment is finished) or a workshop-safety-clearance\ndecision (e.g. declaring a workshop safety-cleared), nor override a\nshop safety officer's judgment -- those decisions must always be a\nhard permanent block, never auto-commit-eligible. This actor is\ndeliberately scoped to WORKSHOP SCHEDULING/LOGISTICS COORDINATION\nONLY -- it never performs garment-construction work or makes\nworkshop-safety-clearance decisions itself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored closely for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7319`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7319)\n(Handicraft Workers Not Elsewhere Classified: `store`/`advisor`/\n`governor`/`actor` split, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set,\nalready landed with a closely-related generic-workshop-craft safety\npattern) -- cloned and read in full in this session. Its `deps.edn`\n`langgraph` git-sha pin was reused verbatim for this repo. 7319's own\nop-allowlist, escalation gates (a hazard-flag op that always escalates,\na supply-order op that escalates above a 2000 cost threshold) and\nscope-exclusion architecture (closed allowlist + defense-in-depth\nfree-text phrase matching) were adopted verbatim in shape, with only\nthe domain vocabulary re-targeted from generic handicraft work to\ntailoring/dressmaking/fur/millinery work.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7531` as an OSS workshop\nscheduling/logistics-coordination actor for tailoring, dressmaking, fur\nand millinery workshops, following the SAME governed-actor architecture\nas every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Stitch\nCoordination Advisor ⊣ StitchCoordGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph`\nStateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned\nidentically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a different library\ncoordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated `20-actors/*`\nactor family), with an independent Governor, human-in-the-loop\napproval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only audit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **workshop scheduling/logistics coordination\nONLY, never direct garment-construction or workshop-safety-clearance\nauthority** -- it must NEVER be designed to exercise, simulate\nexercising, or propose exercising a garment-construction-execution\ndecision (e.g. deciding a garment is finished), a workshop-safety-\nclearance decision (e.g. declaring a workshop safety-cleared), or any\noverride of a shop safety officer's judgment. These are not merely\ngated behind escalation -- they are structurally absent from the\nop-allowlist entirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- job/commission/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a needle-hazard/cutting-tool-\n  hazard/equipment-condition concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER\n  auto-commit eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- fabric/pelt/millinery-materials\n  procurement proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\ngarment-construction-execution decision, a workshop-safety-clearance\ndecision, or a shop-safety-officer-judgment override. These are\n**structurally absent from the op-allowlist entirely**, not merely\ngated behind escalation -- an op such as `:finalize-garment-\nconstruction` cannot even be proposed by the reference mock advisor\n(its `infer`/`rationale-for` functions only ever emit one of the four\nallowlist ops), and if any code path (a forged proposal, a future LLM\nadvisor, a misbehaving fork) ever produced such an op, the governor's\nclosed-allowlist HARD check (`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally\nand permanently. A second, independent HARD check\n(`:scope-excluded-action`) names six concretely-forbidden ops\n(`stitchcoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-garment-construction`,\n`:finalize-garment-construction-execution-decision`,\n`:declare-workshop-safety-cleared`, `:declare-safety-clearance`,\n`:override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`:override-safety-officer-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, and is\nverified by dedicated unit tests\n(`stitchcoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-garment-construction`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-garment-construction-execution-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-workshop-safety-cleared`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-safety-clearance`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-safety-officer-judgment`),\nplus a full-graph-run regression\n(`stitchcoord.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`,\n`.../holds-a-workshop-safety-clearance-op-even-at-high-confidence`,\n`.../holds-an-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment-op-even-at-high-confidence`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Artisan unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered crew-member record (`:no-artisan`). Never\n   trusts the proposal's own claim of who the artisan is.\n2. **Workshop unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an\n   independently registered workshop (`:no-workshop`). Together with\n   check 1, this directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that a\n   worker/workshop record must be independently verified/registered\n   before any action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the six\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for finalizing a garment\n   construction, declaring a workshop safety-clearance, or overriding\n   a shop safety officer's judgment, is a second HARD, PERMANENT block\n   (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated unconditionally on content --\n   defense-in-depth on top of the allowlist check: even if a future\n   change somehow widened the allowlist, content-based rejection still\n   independently blocks garment-construction/workshop-safety-clearance/\n   safety-override language wherever it appears in free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a needle-hazard/\n  cutting-tool-hazard/equipment-condition observation -- it never\n  resolves the concern itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is\n  the hazard data,\" never \"here is what I recommend doing about shop\n  safety.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an over-threshold\n  fabric/pelt/millinery-materials order is not itself unsafe, unlike a\n  garment-construction/workshop-safety-clearance/safety-officer-\n  override attempt, which is why it is handled by a different\n  mechanism (soft escalate vs. structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"needle\", \"pelt\", \"shears\") can accidentally match inside the mock\nadvisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this is exactly the risk\nCLAUDE.md's worked example warns about for this task.\n`stitchcoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is phrased exclusively as\nfinalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"finalize the garment\nconstruction\", \"declare the workshop safety cleared\", \"override the\nshop safety officer's judgment\" -- matching the task's own worked\nexample phrasing verbatim), never bare nouns, and\n`stitchcoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. A second regression test\n(`.../default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-with-cutting-tool-and-pelt-terms`)\ndrives a `:flag-safety-concern` proposal whose task/hazard-type fields\nexplicitly contain the bare nouns \"pelt\", \"shears\" and \"cutting-tool\"\nand confirms it is never hard-blocked (it escalates, as expected for\nany safety concern). The mock advisor's own default rationale template\nwas deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged work\nrecord for artisan ...\", \"scheduled crew operation for tailoring task\n...\", \"... routed for shop safety officer review\") WITHOUT containing\nany of the full finalization-action phrases, so the regression tests\nare a genuine stress test of the bare-noun-vs-action-phrase\ndistinction, not a vacuous pass. Green on first run in this session --\nthe scope-exclusion self-trip guard itself was never tripped during\ndevelopment.\n`stitchcoord.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`,\n`.../holds-a-workshop-safety-clearance-op-even-at-high-confidence` and\n`.../holds-an-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nadditionally exercise the same invariant through the full graph run,\nconfirming a scope-excluded proposal never reaches `commit-record!`\nregardless of disposition path.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7531\" ...}` entry promoted\n  from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id` set to\n  the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7531` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7531`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 28 tests, 61 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-garment-construction` or\n  `:approve-workshop-safety-clearance` that is merely gated behind an\n  always-escalate list: rejected outright per the task's explicit\n  domain-design guidance -- an always-escalate op still means the\n  *capability* to finalize a garment-construction or workshop-safety-\n  clearance decision exists in the code path and is merely deferred to\n  a human gate. For a decision this severe (needle injury, cutting-tool\n  injury, product-quality clearance, workshop-safety clearance), the\n  capability itself must not exist. The only op related to shop-safety\n  escalation is `:flag-safety-concern`, which surfaces the need for\n  human/shop-safety-officer attention and never itself decides,\n  authorizes, or defers a garment-construction or workshop-safety-\n  clearance decision for later automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block: rejected per the task's\n  explicit domain design -- an over-threshold fabric/pelt/millinery-\n  materials order is not itself unsafe, so it is handled as a soft\n  escalate gate, not a hard block; only the garment-construction/\n  workshop-safety-clearance/safety-officer-override class is a hard,\n  unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"needle\" \"pelt\"\n  \"shears\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked example for this\n  exact task), and per the explicit instruction to phrase\n  scope-exclusion terms as finalization/execution ACTIONS, never bare\n  nouns -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses needle/\n  cutting-tool/pelt/safety-officer concepts to do its scheduling/\n  logging job, so a bare-noun list would risk self-blocking the\n  actor's own legitimate proposals (regression-tested directly against\n  rationale/task/hazard-type text that deliberately contains those\n  bare nouns).\n- Adopting a single dominant hazard type (e.g. modeling only a\n  needle-injury risk and omitting cutting-tool or equipment-condition\n  hazards): rejected -- 7531 spans four related trades (tailors,\n  dressmakers, furriers, hatters) that share needle, cutting-tool\n  (shears) and sewing-machine/equipment hazards without one dominant\n  type, so `:hazard-type` stays a free-form field with generic\n  examples (needle-hazard / cutting-tool-hazard / equipment-condition)\n  rather than a single hardcoded dominant hazard.\n- Giving the actor an autonomous pelt/fur material-provenance\n  verification or certification op: rejected -- the task's domain\n  design scopes this actor to workshop scheduling/logistics\n  coordination only; provenance and sourcing determinations for pelt\n  materials are a workshop-registration and human-judgment concern, not\n  an automatable op, so `:coordinate-supply-order` treats fabric/pelt/\n  millinery-materials orders identically (proposal + cost-threshold\n  escalation), with no separate provenance-clearance capability.\n- Merging `artisan` and `workshop` into a single entity (only checking\n  one provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity provenance shape\n  (independently-registered artisan AND independently-registered\n  workshop) matches the CRITICAL invariant that a \"worker/workshop\n  record must be independently verified/registered before any action\"\n  and the established pattern from prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors\n  with two-sided provenance checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- job/commission/progress data logging\n   only. Requires an independently registered artisan AND workshop\n   (`:no-artisan`/`:no-workshop`). Not a garment-construction or\n   workshop-safety-clearance decision in any respect -- it is a\n   records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n   only. Cannot carry a garment-construction-execution decision\n   (structurally absent from the op's field shape; any such attempt\n   via free text is caught by the `:scope-excluded-action` content\n   check). Does not authorize, finalize, or draw any conclusion about a\n   specific garment -- it is a calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a needle-hazard/cutting-\n   tool-hazard/equipment-condition concern to a human/shop safety\n   officer; ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at every confidence\n   level, NEVER auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through\n   which a safety observation may be surfaced, and it explicitly never\n   resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself -- the shop safety\n   officer reviews and acts entirely on their own authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- fabric/pelt/millinery-materials\n   procurement proposal only (item, cost). Not a garment-construction\n   or workshop-safety-clearance decision of any kind -- it is a\n   purchasing-logistics action, gated by ordinary cost-ceiling\n   escalation (above 2000 always escalates), regardless of whether the\n   material is fabric, pelt or millinery trim.\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na garment-construction-execution decision (e.g. deciding a garment is\nfinished), a workshop-safety-clearance decision (e.g. declaring a\nworkshop safety-cleared), or a shop-safety-officer-judgment override --\nthese categories are structurally absent, not gated, confirmed by: (a)\nthe closed four-op allowlist itself (`stitchcoord.governor/allowed-ops`),\n(b) six concretely-named forbidden-op fixtures rejected at the\ngovernor-unit level (`stitchcoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`stitchcoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-garment-construction`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-garment-construction-execution-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-workshop-safety-cleared`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-safety-clearance`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-safety-officer-judgment`), and\n(c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op`\nfield (`stitchcoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to finalize a garment construction, declare a workshop\nsafety cleared, or override a shop safety officer's judgment even via\nan otherwise-allowlisted op\n(`stitchcoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-even-with-allowlisted-op`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-declare-workshop-safety-cleared`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-shop-safety-officer`).\n", :adr/date "2026-07-18", :actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}", :test/counts "{:total 28, :assertions 61, :failures 0, :errors 0}", :actor/coordination? true, :actor/name "Tailoring Workshop Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Practice", :db/id -1, :test/coverage [:governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :artisan-verification :workshop-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation], :registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7531", :registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7531", :adr/scope [:kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7531], :test/simulator :stitchcoord.actor-test, :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7531 — Tailors, Dressmakers, Furriers and Hatters Workshop Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/references [2607121000], :actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7531}]
